  "upload": {
    "title": "How Do You Dig a Tunnel Without Stopping? 🚇 #shorts",
    "description": "This machine digs a tunnel and builds it at the same time. 🚇\n\nMost tunnel boring machines work in cycles: dig, stop, install a concrete ring, then dig again. The Boring Company's Prufrock mines continuously: the cutterhead grinds through rock at the front while concrete liner segments are placed right behind it, and the spoil rides out on a conveyor belt the whole time. The machines are monitored and controlled remotely from the company's operations center in Bastrop, Texas.\n\nDigging tunnels to escape traffic, while working from home. 👇\n\nSubscribe to Top Techs for more mind-blowing tech in under a minute.",
